 * AUTO-GENERATED by can_bus/canoe/generate_capl.py. Do not edit by hand; rerun the script
 * after changing can_bus/hexray/*.json. Generated from: can_bus/hexray @ 1f03956bd
 *
 * Setup:
 *   - Add hexray_canoe.dbc to the CANoe configuration and assign it to every channel below.
 *   - FDCAN: 1000 kbit/s, CAN FD, BRS off (data rate = arbitration rate) -> CH_FDCAN
 *   - InvCAN: 1000 kbit/s, classic CAN -> CH_INVCAN
 *   - charger: 500 kbit/s, classic CAN -> CH_CHARGER
 *   - Add this file as a CAPL node in the Simulation Setup (any channel; each send sets .CAN).
 *   - Set gSim_<Node> = 0 for every node that is real hardware on the bench.
 *
 * Timing mirrors the firmware: every periodic message is sent at each multiple of its
 * GenMsgCycleTime from measurement start, on the bus(es) its owner sends it on. When a
 * forwarding node (VC, BMS) is simulated it also forwards the messages it reroutes in the
 * firmware, both from simulated nodes and from real hardware.
 * Signals start at GenSigStartValue; every <Node>_Heartbeat is driven to 1.
 */

